  "id": "symbolic-mode",
  "term": "symbolic mode",
  "definition": "Symbolic mode is a way of using a language mainly as a sign of cultural identity and belonging rather than primarily as a practical literacy skill. In the source, it describes heritage-language use in family, peer, and emotional contexts that helps maintain identity even when literacy proficiency is limited.",
